I did it - i cannot believe that this is true. I beat Nethack!
Here is the long diary of a lonely human neutral Barbarian named
Hektor.

Having heard rumors of a valkyrie who choked to death in Gehenom, i
started by promising not to eat too much and to reduce stupid moves to
a minimum. It all started out very nice. Early altars (two on lvl2,
one on lvl4 -the level with the branch to the mines) granted me a nice
sharp axe - the Cleaver and ensured a steady supply of holy water.
I went with Jack the Ripper (my nice dog) into the Gnomish Mines and
quickly found some good armor (+2 dwarvish iron helm, +2 boots and an
elven mithril coat. The town had a crossaligned priest, but since Jack
was killed by something in the Mines, i had to do some fighting
myself  was XL6 when reaching the mines and not able to buy
protection. Happy with swinging the axe, i went on to find the
luckstone. Reached the bottom of the Mines without meeting polymorphed
Gnomes or other serious fighters and went back up.
Not able to part from unidentified potions and other stuff, i was
burdened most of the time from now on. Went back to the main dungeon
and found a new dog on the Delphi level. Found a polymorph trap and
dragged the dog onto it with a leash, but things got worse with each
polymorphing the dog went through: dog - tengu - elf Mummy - kobold
shaman - grid bug. Needless to say, that pet did not survive for long.
Reached the BigRoom without having found Sokoban. Escaped back up and
took a little dog with me. Found sokoban and solved it, carefully
growing the little Hitaki into a large one. Went through the Zoo on
the top level without bigger problems and got Reflection. Would have
preferred the BoH, because burdening was still a serious problem.
Now having collected lots of gold, i wanted to buy my first points of
protection in Minetown. AC -4 was ok, but not great. On the way back
up, Hitaki polymorphed into a red Dragon. Playing with the
"intelligent pet patch", Hitaki invoked chaos in Minetown, killing
shopkeepers and watchmen alike with his fiery breath. I kept him away
from the priest and with all the gold, i could donate to the priest
thrice, giving me 5 points of protection. Cleared out the shops, found
2 cursed magic lamps, uncursed them and used a first wish for BoH.
Finally got unburdened. Decided to keep the other one for emergencies.
Returned to the BigRoom and smashed many monsters. Found a T-Shirt.
Was shocked to stumble over the cadaver of Hitaki some levels deeper.
Found another altar on lvl18 and read a cursed create-monster scroll.
Went well until a nymph stole the cleaver, but at this point, most of
the monsters were killed anyway.
Turn 28000, lvl 25. Still have not arrived at the castle. Still no
magic resistance, levitation, polymorph or other nice things until
now. Not even a magic whistle. Fought my first 2 dragons (green and
gray) in a throne room. Luckily, i had a scroll of eA which gave me
the direly needed GDSM. New AC (with enchanted T-Shirt) is -18. Still
- no conflict, freeAction, levitation, or speedboots.
lvl26 was the medusa level. Without means to cross the water, i
decided to go back and do the quest.
Back on lvl24, i encountered a succubus from a drain. With
intelligence 8 and ch 6, this was not as pleasing as i expected it to
be. Found a cloak of displacement which replaced my elven cloak.
The quest was difficult without a pet to eat all the Trolls. Entered
the final room. Drew back and thought "i could make myself invisible
and sneak past the trolls." So i zapped myself with a wand and became
PERMANENTLY invisible. That was not was i expected. Recovered the
Heart and went back to the main dungeon.
Found a dog who transformed into a baby black dragon. Did not survive
very long - you hear a nearby zap - you have a sad feeling for a
moment. I think i have just found my first /oDeath. Have never been so
happy to see a friend getting killed.
Invoked the Heart to fly to Medusas home. Reached the castle and had
fun smashing Liches under the drawbridge. Used the wishes for speed
boots and gauntlets of power and saved the rest of the wishes.
Arrived at molochs altar and went back up to collect the money i left
in some chests. On the way back down, i encountered a lonely nurse in
the castle. She raised my hp to 240 (thanks to some alchemy i startet
nurse-dancing at 220)
Bought two more points of protection (7 total). Together with another ?
oEA, my new AC is now -22. Lets go killing some demon princes.
DL31, first maze level. The Disintegration blast whizzes by you while
i was wearing ESP instead of reflection. Too satiated to safely eat
his corpse :(
37000, Lvl 35 - Jubilex. No challenge. Invoked heart carries me over
the water. Still have not found a genoscroll to get rid of the purple
Ls. 3 wishes + magic lamp look nice, though. Used up a whish for 2
genoscrolls. Unsure of what to do with the last two wishes. =Conflict?
MagicMarker? Helm of Brilliance? =FreeAction?
38100 - the Vampire reads a (cursed) scroll of create monster. Hello
Disenchanter. Hello Black Dragon. Hello Nazgul. Hello leocrotta. This
is going to be tough. First action was cancelling the disenchanter.
After that, the fight was easier as expected. Ate the dragon and
gained disintegration resistance. Faced Asmodeus and his nurse.
The demon princes kept teleporting away, so i did not deal with them.
DL39 had a tower. Never got so far before. Finally a place to drop all
those surplus wands. Found the first "oLS not worn by creatures. Yeah.
The owner seems to have his personal zoo here, with creepy monsters
locked into single small cells. Found him. Vlad the Impaler. Not a big
fighter. He dropped a candelabrum. I attached some candles i found
earlier to it.
41.000 identified ring of levitation
42k. Met a vampire with a /oDeath. Could fire 4 times before i got
him. Orcus met a paralyse-potion and i got a third /oD. Weee. Found
the Demonbane on the same level. Now this is really strange - The
Demonbane waiting in midst of several demons.
Dlvl44 - Found the sunsword but decided to not use it.
43300 - found a maze with an area i could not enter. The famous Wizard
of Yendor was there.
Dlvl50. Strange. No stairs down in the level. Still did not find the
Amulet. Looks like i have to go back up, exploring the mazes where i
found the next stairs very quick.
Dlvl49. Found a small island with a useless amulet on it.
46200 - finally found a wand of polymorph on lvl 48. Hope to get some
more ?eA and a ring of conflict from it. Same level had another small
island with a magic portal on it. It took me two levels up, into a
central region. In the middle there was another island which i could
now cross with the ring of levitation. Climbed up the ladder.
Telepathy showed a very crowded room before me. An identify-scroll and
some alchemy later (now lvl17, HP 279) i entered the room. Put on my
towel after an Umber Hulk confused me. Some hours of fighting later
(never got below 200 HP thanks to my =oRegen, i collected 9k zorkmids
and dropped them elsewhere.
Not daring to go up, i decided to do some polymorphing before facing
the evil wizard. After some useless rounds of fun with a succubus, i
entered his hall.
He created a doubleganger of himself, but my +4 Cleaver could take
them down. He dropped a book, which i read. Whee! You raised the dead.
So - what now? I have explored everything i could and still no way to
go on.
Read a spoiler and found out about the vibrating square. Ok, lets try
to find it.
Hey.. My inventory is getting cursed with the time. Whats that?
Found the square and performed the ritual. Impressive effect :)
Chaos. Madness. Crazy stuff happening. Two wizards of Yendor stealing
my stuff and engaging the Priestress of Moloch. They were mad at me
and attacked me. Could grab the Amulet and ran upwards. Somewhere on
lvl 41, the wizard stole the amulet and disappeared.
49400 - After a lot of wizard-killing, i finally reached the altar
below the castle
50100 , lvl 22. Dropped the amulet and boosted up my armor with 4
blessed scrolls. New AC: -32, but not every item fire/rustproofed.
Found a magic marker. On lvl18, another altar. Some rounds of
polymorphing later, i had the ring of conflict i wanted.
50600, lvl4, still havent met the wizard again. Enchanted my silver
saber and frost brand to +4, switching to twoweaponing. Felt save and
decided to do some training in longsword by summoning some critters.
Went to basic. Still two wishes left.
Dlvl1. Returned with the amulet. What will happen? End game. The
Wizard again. Meet my rubber chicken, evil one :-) Now what. I am in a
very small dark room with no doors. Telepathy shows many monsters
around. Wearing ring of conflict now.
Reached skilled status in longsword and went to twoweaponing. What is
this level. No corridors, no stairs. Magic mapping does not help.
Wished for a blessed crystal ball to search for the portal. Did not
work. Used wands of digging and stumbled through the level until i
accidently stepped on a magic portal.
On the next level, i used confused gold detection to find the portal.
Big Fun. Conflict let me pass by the hordes on most levels. Used a
cursed ?oConfusion as replacement for booze on Water level. One wish
left was spent on an "oLS. Water plane was a strange experience. Used
a genoscroll for ; because i did not want to meet these guys in their
natural element. Prepared myself for a last big fight - 8 death charges
+b?charging, 5 blessed taming-scrolls+2confusion
42 marker charges left. Extincted Rs. Waiting for the bubble to float
to the portal
at around 200/300 HP i arrive at the first, rightmost altar. What a
chaos. Lawful altar. Up to the next one, through 200 ants and insects.
With 2 priests and Pestilence lined up in a row, i used my WoD.
Arrived the central gate with nearly full HP thanks to my =Regen. With
Death Guarding the central stage, i decided to try the leftmost altar
now. Zapped Famine. Chaotic altar. Wrong again. Famine and Death
incoming, one next to another. I fear fighting Death. Zapped Famine
and tried to run away from Death. Dancing around a giant beetle, the
maneuver really worked :) Famine reincarnated behind me, and with
Pestilence still beeing stuck in a swarm of insects, the way was
nearly free to the central altar. Offering the Amulet, i was granted
the status of a Demigod.


----------

Thats it. It was an incredibly great experience.
After the game i learned in #nethack on the IRC that i would have
needed a patch to create the gamedump files most people are posting
here. No info about score, killed monsters or anything else.

game-influencing patches used:
- "intelligent-pet" patch  -- made the game somewhat easier (the
dragon in Minetown was cool) but i still like it
- "banes enhancement" - Demonbane was really useful when engaging the
demonic princes.
- "consistent hole endpoints" - another patch i don't want to miss.

On to the second ascension :-)
